<title>FINLAND: NOKIA SAYS UPM VOTE AT 6.71 PCT.</title>
<headline>NOKIA SAYS UPM VOTE AT 6.71 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish telecoms group Nokia said Finnish forestry group UPM-Kymmene Oy's reduction of its holding in Nokia would take its stake below seven percent from Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;UPM-Kymmene sells 4,500,000 A shares which decreases the number of Nokia shares held by UPM-Kymmene to 2.39 percent and of the corresponding voting rights to 6.71 percent,&quot; Nokia said in a statement.</p>
<p>UPM Kymmene said last week it had sold 4.5 million Nokia shares. Due to conversion of shares, Nokia said UPM's voting rights fell below 10 percent. It was 7.14 percent on June 30.</p>
